A LinkedList is a collection where elements are stored as nodes, and each node is connected to the next node. It is useful when we frequently add or remove elements.


ArrayList:
add()
get()
remove()

LinkedList:
add()
addFirst()
addLast()
remove()

HashMap:
put()
get()
remove()

Queue:
add()
peek()
poll()

Stack:
push()
peek()
pop()

exmaples:
    import java.util.LinkedList;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        LinkedList<String> names = new LinkedList<>();

        names.add("Javed");
        names.add("Rahul");
        names.add("Aman");

        System.out.println(names);

        names.addFirst("John");
        names.remove("Rahul");

        System.out.println(names);
    }
}

o/p:    [Javed, Rahul, Aman]
[John, Javed, Aman]










